content:
{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "future_dated",
      "files": [
        "05_master_data/Cost Centres and Budgets FY2026-27.xlsx"
      ],
      "detail": "Cost centre PRD-09 includes a future-dated budget allocation of £865,000 for period 2027-Q1 starting 1 January 2027."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "duplicate",
      "files": [
        "01_policies/POL-SUP-003 Supplier Policy v2.3.pdf",
        "01_policies/POL-SUP-003 Supplier Policy v2.3 (1).pdf"
      ],
      "detail": "POL-SUP-003 Supplier Policy v2.3 (1).pdf is a duplicate file of POL-SUP-003 Supplier Policy v2.3.pdf."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-AP-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Accounts Payable v7.2.3.pdf",
        "04_service_definitions/accounts_payable/bnk_block.xml",
        "04_service_definitions/accounts_payable/bnk_get.xml"
      ],
      "detail": "MAN-AP-72 defines ERR-BNK-0001 as missing mandatory settlement routing fields during bnk_save, whereas the backend service definitions for bnk_block and bnk_get define it as 'SUPPLIER BANK DETAILS NOT FOUND'."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "duplicate",
      "files": [
        "01_policies/POL-SUP-003 Supplier Policy v2.3 (1).pdf",
        "01_policies/POL-SUP-003 Supplier Policy v2.3.pdf"
      ],
      "detail": "POL-SUP-003 Supplier Policy v2.3 (1).pdf is an identical duplicate copy of POL-SUP-003 Supplier Policy v2.3.pdf."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "findings": [
    {"kind": "inconsistent_naming", "files": ["07_data_dictionary/Ledgerline_7.2_tables_and_fields.xlsx", "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-ERR-72 Message and Error Code Reference v7.2.3.pdf"], "detail": "The 'See also' link label for [[err-apr-0004]] describes the error as 'Advance amount exceeds PO unbilled commitment', which conflicts with the actual message 'VALUE ABOVE YOUR LIMIT'."}
  ]
}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-AP-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Accounts Payable v7.2.3.pdf",
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-ERR-72 Message and Error Code Reference v7.2.3.pdf"
      ],
      "detail": "MAN-AP-72 defines ERR-BNK-0101 as indicating that BANK CD does not match an active disbursement account in GL master tables or the selected account is suspended, whereas MAN-ERR-72 (along with MAN-AP-72 §20 and the data dictionary) defines it as 'BANK DETAILS NOT VERIFIED (<sup_cd>)' raised during payment approval or filing."
    }
  ]
}

{"findings": [
  {"kind": "contradiction", "files": ["05_master_data/Cost Centres and Budgets FY2026-27.xlsx", "09_email_archive/2026/2026-10-01_Spring launch run - cost centre PRD-07.eml", "10_meeting_notes/2026-09-30 S&OP meeting.docx"], "detail": "The meeting notes and email state that cost centre PRD-07 opened effective 1 October 2026, but Cost Centres and Budgets FY2026-27.xlsx lists quarterly budgets and commitments for PRD-07 spanning 2025-Q1 through 2026-Q3."},
  {"kind": "contradiction", "files": ["05_master_data/Cost Centres and Budgets FY2026-27.xlsx", "06_transactions/PO_extract_2026-01_to_2026-10.xlsx", "06_transactions/reports/PO register 2026-10 (printed).pdf"], "detail": "Cost Centres and Budgets FY2026-27.xlsx records 2026-Q4 committed spend for PRD-07 as £310,000, whereas the PO extract and PO register show October 2026 purchase order commitments against PRD-07 exceeding £3,000,000 across PO/2026/01167, PO/2026/01178, and PO/2026/01179."}
]}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "07_data_dictionary/Ledgerline_7.2_tables_and_fields.xlsx",
        "04_service_definitions/inventory/adj_approve.yaml",
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-INV-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Inventory v7.2.3.pdf"
      ],
      "detail": "The data dictionary and adj_approve service define ERR-ADJ-0420 as exceeding the Stores role limit requiring Plant Head approval, whereas MAN-INV-72 defines ERR-ADJ-0420 as a negative adjustment quantity exceeding available physical stock in the warehouse location."
    },
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "07_data_dictionary/Ledgerline_7.2_tables_and_fields.xlsx",
        "04_service_definitions/inventory/adj_cancel.yaml",
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-INV-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Inventory v7.2.3.pdf"
      ],
      "detail": "The data dictionary and adj_cancel service define ERR-ADJ-0801 as attempting an action on an already-closed stock adjustment, whereas MAN-INV-72 defines ERR-ADJ-0801 as an unrecognised value entered in REASON CD."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SAL-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Sales and Distribution v7.2.3.pdf",
        "04_service_definitions/sales/alc_cancel.yaml",
        "04_service_definitions/sales/alc_get.yaml"
      ],
      "detail": "MAN-SAL-72 defines ERR-ALC-0001 as indicating a sales order cannot be found or is in an invalid status, whereas alc_cancel.yaml and alc_get.yaml define it as 'ALLOCATION NOT FOUND' when an allocation record cannot be identified."
    },
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SAL-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Sales and Distribution v7.2.3.pdf",
        "04_service_definitions/sales/alc_cancel.yaml"
      ],
      "detail": "MAN-SAL-72 defines ERR-ALC-0801 as an allocation run failure due to insufficient pickable stock, quarantine hold, or locked records, whereas alc_cancel.yaml defines it as attempting to cancel an already closed allocation ('ALLOCATION CLOSED (<status>)')."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SAL-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Sales and Distribution v7.2.3.pdf",
        "04_service_definitions/sales/fcs_get.yaml"
      ],
      "detail": "MAN-SAL-72 documents ERR-FCS-0001 as raised by fcs_save for missing mandatory fields, closed periods, or database locks, whereas the fcs_get service definition specifies it is raised by fcs_get when a sales forecast ID is not found."
    },
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SAL-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Sales and Distribution v7.2.3.pdf",
        "04_service_definitions/sales/fcs_save.yaml",
        "04_service_definitions/sales/fcs_upload.yaml"
      ],
      "detail": "MAN-SAL-72 defines ERR-FCS-0201 as raised by fcs_get for missing forecast records or closed periods, whereas service definitions for fcs_save and fcs_upload define it as raised when forecast quantity is not greater than zero."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-AP-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Accounts Payable v7.2.3.pdf",
        "07_data_dictionary/Ledgerline_7.2_tables_and_fields.xlsx"
      ],
      "detail": "MAN-AP-72 defines ERR-MAT-0410, ERR-MAT-0411, ERR-MAT-0412, and ERR-MAT-0420 inconsistently between the AP-MAT-02 screen message reference on page 9 and the general system error definitions in Section 20 and the data dictionary."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-ERR-72 Message and Error Code Reference v7.2.3.pdf",
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SAL-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Sales and Distribution v7.2.3.pdf"
      ],
      "detail": "MAN-ERR-72 (and service definitions) defines ERR-RMA-0001 as indicating a warranty return was not found, whereas MAN-SAL-72 states ERR-RMA-0001 indicates missing mandatory header data before rma_save can generate a tracking file."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SAL-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Sales and Distribution v7.2.3.pdf",
        "04_service_definitions/sales/quo_cancel.yaml",
        "04_service_definitions/sales/quo_convert.yaml",
        "04_service_definitions/sales/quo_get.yaml"
      ],
      "detail": "MAN-SAL-72 states ERR-QUO-0001 is raised when mandatory header fields are incomplete during saving, whereas service definitions specify it indicates 'QUOTATION NOT FOUND' during quo_cancel, quo_convert, and quo_get operations."
    },
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SAL-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Sales and Distribution v7.2.3.pdf",
        "04_service_definitions/sales/quo_save.yaml",
        "04_service_definitions/sales/quo_search.yaml"
      ],
      "detail": "MAN-SAL-72 defines ERR-QUO-0201 as raised when a quotation cannot be converted due to VALID TO being earlier than the current date, whereas service definitions define it as 'QTY MUST BE > 0' raised by quo_save and quo_search."
    },
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SAL-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Sales and Distribution v7.2.3.pdf",
        "04_service_definitions/sales/quo_cancel.yaml"
      ],
      "detail": "MAN-SAL-72 states ERR-QUO-0801 is raised when REASON is missing during quo_cancel or when saving with a restricted customer account, whereas quo_cancel.yaml defines it as 'QUOTATION CLOSED (<status>)' when attempting to cancel an already closed quotation."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "05_master_data/ITEM_MASTER_2026-10-26.xlsx",
        "06_transactions/reports/Item master listing 2026-10 (printed).pdf"
      ],
      "detail": "ITEM_MASTER_2026-10-26 records lead days for BEL-STD-01 as 21, whereas Item master listing 2026-10 records lead days (LC) as 0."
    }
  ]
}

{"findings": [
  {"kind": "contradiction", "files": ["03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SAL-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Sales and Distribution v7.2.3.pdf", "04_service_definitions/sales/edi_ord_in.xml", "12_integrations/EDI ORDERS interface spec v2.1.pdf"], "detail": "MAN-SAL-72 defines ERR-EDI-0140 as a message syntax or mapping error from corrupted records, invalid tags, or missing customer trade parameters, whereas edi_ord_in.xml and INT-EDI-001 define it as an unknown buyer item code not mapped in the customer cross-reference table."},
  {"kind": "contradiction", "files": ["03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SAL-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Sales and Distribution v7.2.3.pdf", "04_service_definitions/sales/edi_ord_in.xml"], "detail": "MAN-SAL-72 defines ERR-EDI-0150 as outbound document generation halted due to missing sales ledger data or failed network handshaking, whereas edi_ord_in.xml defines it as a syntax error in an inbound message segment."}
]}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SAL-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Sales and Distribution v7.2.3.pdf",
        "04_service_definitions/sales/sinv_cancel.yaml",
        "04_service_definitions/sales/sinv_get.yaml",
        "04_service_definitions/sales/sinv_post.yaml",
        "04_service_definitions/sales/sinv_print.yaml"
      ],
      "detail": "MAN-SAL-72 defines ERR-SIN-0001 as indicating an invalid, incomplete, or already invoiced delivery reference in DLV NO, whereas the backend service definitions define it as SALES INVOICE NOT FOUND."
    },
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SAL-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Sales and Distribution v7.2.3.pdf",
        "04_service_definitions/sales/sinv_post.yaml"
      ],
      "detail": "MAN-SAL-72 defines ERR-SIN-0007 as a locked sales invoice record due to closed financial periods, customer locks, or missing nominal/tax codes, whereas sinv_post defines it as SALES INVOICE NOT IN DRAFT (<status>)."
    },
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SAL-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Sales and Distribution v7.2.3.pdf",
        "04_service_definitions/sales/sinv_cancel.yaml"
      ],
      "detail": "MAN-SAL-72 defines ERR-SIN-0801 as missing cancellation reason, cancellation of an invoice cleared by cash allocation, or posting in a closed period, whereas sinv_cancel defines it as SALES INVOICE CLOSED (<status>)."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "findings": [
    {"kind": "superseded", "files": ["03_ledgerline_manuals/old/MAN-INV-72 Inventory v7.2.2 (old).pdf", "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-INV-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Inventory v7.2.3.pdf"], "detail": "The page references and cites old/MAN-INV-72 Inventory v7.2.2 (old).pdf for active sections and screen functionality (including INV-WHS-01, INV-ITM-01, INV-CCP-14, INV-QCH-11, INV-RES-12, INV-KBN-13, INV-PKG-15, INV-SCR-16, INV-CSG-17, and INV-STK-03) which are already incorporated into the current v7.2.3 manual."}
  ]
}

{"findings": [
  {"kind": "contradiction", "files": ["07_data_dictionary/Ledgerline_7.2_tables_and_fields.xlsx", "04_service_definitions/inventory/txf_cancel.yaml", "04_service_definitions/inventory/txf_get.yaml", "04_service_definitions/inventory/txf_post.yaml", "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-INV-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Inventory v7.2.3.pdf"], "detail": "The data dictionary and service definitions define ERR-TXF-0001 as 'STOCK TRANSFER NOT FOUND' raised by txf_get, txf_post, and txf_cancel, whereas MAN-INV-72 documents it as raised by txf_save when mandatory fields (ITEM CD, FROM WHS, TO WHS, QTY) are omitted."},
  {"kind": "contradiction", "files": ["07_data_dictionary/Ledgerline_7.2_tables_and_fields.xlsx", "04_service_definitions/inventory/txf_post.yaml", "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-INV-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Inventory v7.2.3.pdf"], "detail": "The data dictionary and txf_post service definition define ERR-TXF-0007 as 'STOCK TRANSFER NOT IN DRAFT (<status>)', whereas MAN-INV-72 documents it as raised when FROM WHS and TO WHS specify identical locations on screen INV-TRF-04."},
  {"kind": "contradiction", "files": ["07_data_dictionary/Ledgerline_7.2_tables_and_fields.xlsx", "04_service_definitions/inventory/txf_save.yaml", "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-INV-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Inventory v7.2.3.pdf"], "detail": "The data dictionary and txf_save service definition define ERR-TXF-0201 as 'QTY MUST BE > 0', whereas MAN-INV-72 states it is raised when a transfer record is locked by another network user."},
  {"kind": "contradiction", "files": ["07_data_dictionary/Ledgerline_7.2_tables_and_fields.xlsx", "04_service_definitions/inventory/txf_save.yaml", "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-INV-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Inventory v7.2.3.pdf"], "detail": "The data dictionary and txf_save service definition define ERR-TXF-0310 as 'FROM AND TO WAREHOUSE ARE THE SAME', whereas MAN-INV-72 documents it as indicating the selected transfer has already been posted or cancelled and cannot be altered."},
  {"kind": "contradiction", "files": ["07_data_dictionary/Ledgerline_7.2_tables_and_fields.xlsx", "04_service_definitions/inventory/txf_cancel.yaml", "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-INV-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Inventory v7.2.3.pdf"], "detail": "The data dictionary and txf_cancel service definition define ERR-TXF-0801 as 'STOCK TRANSFER CLOSED (<status>)', whereas MAN-INV-72 documents it as a general posting failure or an invalid cancellation attempt on an already committed or cancelled transfer."}
]}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "duplicate",
      "files": [
        "01_policies/POL-SUP-003 Supplier Policy v2.3 (1).pdf",
        "01_policies/POL-SUP-003 Supplier Policy v2.3.pdf"
      ],
      "detail": "POL-SUP-003 Supplier Policy v2.3 (1).pdf is an identical duplicate copy of POL-SUP-003 Supplier Policy v2.3.pdf."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "rule_not_in_policy",
      "files": [
        "01_policies/POL-QUA-005 Quality Policy v3.0.pdf",
        "10_meeting_notes/2026-08-21 Quality meeting.docx"
      ],
      "detail": "Operational quality controls such as frame alignment checks, down tube deburring, tamper-evident lacquer on motor brackets, fork protector strapping, and the immediate Ledgerline quarantine routine exist only in meeting notes and are not formally codified in POL-QUA-005."
    },
    {
      "kind": "rule_not_in_policy",
      "files": [
        "01_policies/POL-QUA-005 Quality Policy v3.0.pdf",
        "09_email_archive/2019/2019-12-04_Quarantine bin full.eml",
        "09_email_archive/2021/2021-06-27_ISO 9001 surveillance audit.eml"
      ],
      "detail": "Rules regarding ISO 9001 audit preparations, yellow quarantine status labels, and clearing paperwork for supplier returns against delivery notes are derived only from emails and are not documented in POL-QUA-005."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-AP-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Accounts Payable v7.2.3.pdf",
        "04_service_definitions/accounts_payable/sbal_query.yaml"
      ],
      "detail": "MAN-AP-72 states that both SUP CD and AS ON must be populated before querying and that a missing AS ON triggers ERR-SBL-0001, whereas sbal_query.yaml defines both sup_cd and as_on as optional parameters."
    }
  ]
}

{"findings": [
  {
    "kind": "contradiction",
    "files": [
      "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SCR-72 Screen Reference v7.2.3.pdf",
      "04_service_definitions/accounts_payable/inv_hold.yaml"
    ],
    "detail": "MAN-SCR-72 lists REASON as a mandatory field on AP-INV-01 (including when placing a voucher on query hold), whereas the inv_hold service definition specifies reason as optional."
  },
  {
    "kind": "contradiction",
    "files": [
      "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SCR-72 Screen Reference v7.2.3.pdf",
      "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-AP-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Accounts Payable v7.2.3.pdf",
      "04_service_definitions/accounts_payable/inv_save.yaml"
    ],
    "detail": "MAN-SCR-72 and inv_save.yaml define ERR-INV-0118 as 'Duplicate Supplier Invoice No', whereas MAN-AP-72 states that duplicate supplier invoice numbers raise ERR-INV-0007 upon save and ERR-INV-0118 indicates incomplete lines or blank mandatory fields when posting."
  },
  {
    "kind": "contradiction",
    "files": [
      "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-AP-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Accounts Payable v7.2.3.pdf"
    ],
    "detail": "MAN-AP-72 internally contradicts itself on the status assigned after saving on AP-INV-01, stating in the step-by-step procedure that STATUS is set to 'draft', but stating in the questions section that STATUS is set to 'unposted'."
  }
]}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-INV-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Inventory v7.2.3.pdf",
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SCR-72 Screen Reference v7.2.3.pdf"
      ],
      "detail": "MAN-INV-72 specifies that the descr (DESCRIPTION) field on screen INV-ITM-01 is mandatory, whereas MAN-SCR-72 lists it as optional."
    }
  ]
}

{"findings": [
  {
    "kind": "contradiction",
    "files": [
      "01_policies/POL-APR-002 Approval Matrix v3.0.pdf",
      "01_policies/POL-PUR-001_Purchase_Policy_v4.1.pdf"
    ],
    "detail": "POL-APR-002 states that a document within the raiser's own approval limit is approved upon submission with the raiser recorded as approver, whereas POL-PUR-001 §5.3 and POL-APR-002 §4 state that no user may approve a document they raised regardless of limit."
  }
]}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "02_procedures/SOP-AP-002 Period Close v3.0.pdf",
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SCR-72 Screen Reference v7.2.3.pdf",
        "04_service_definitions/accounts_payable/per_close.yaml",
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-AP-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Accounts Payable v7.2.3.pdf"
      ],
      "detail": "The service definitions, screen reference, and SOP-AP-002 define ERR-PER-0010 as unposted documents remaining and ERR-PER-0011 as GRNI accrual not run, whereas the AP user manual describes ERR-PER-0010 as opening an already open/sealed period or closing a closed interval, and ERR-PER-0011 as closing a closed/unopened period or opening an invalid interval."
    },
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SCR-72 Screen Reference v7.2.3.pdf",
        "04_service_definitions/accounts_payable/per_close.yaml",
        "04_service_definitions/accounts_payable/per_status.yaml",
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-AP-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Accounts Payable v7.2.3.pdf"
      ],
      "detail": "ERR-PER-0001 is defined across service definitions and reference manuals as period identifier not found or blank, but MAN-AP-72 worked examples state that per_status halts with ERR-PER-0001 if unposted purchase batches remain pending."
    },
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SCR-72 Screen Reference v7.2.3.pdf",
        "04_service_definitions/accounts_payable/per_close.yaml",
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-AP-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Accounts Payable v7.2.3.pdf"
      ],
      "detail": "ERR-PER-0801 is defined in the service definition and screen reference as period closed, whereas the MAN-AP-72 user manual states it signals unposted purchase ledger transactions preventing closing or insufficient user authorisation rights."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-PUR-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Purchasing v7.2.3.pdf",
        "04_service_definitions/purchase/stk_query.yaml"
      ],
      "detail": "MAN-PUR-72 states that days of cover on INV-STK-02 is calculated as on-hand divided by average daily issue, whereas stk_query.yaml defines it as (on_hand - allocated) divided by average daily issue."
    },
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SCR-72 Screen Reference v7.2.3.pdf",
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-PUR-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Purchasing v7.2.3.pdf",
        "04_service_definitions/purchase/stk_query.yaml",
        "11_training/QRC-08 Stock enquiry and days of cover.pdf"
      ],
      "detail": "MAN-SCR-72 lists the warehouse field whs_cd as mandatory on INV-STK-02, whereas MAN-PUR-72, stk_query.yaml, and QRC-08 define it as optional."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "duplicate",
      "files": [
        "01_policies/POL-SUP-003 Supplier Policy v2.3 (1).pdf",
        "01_policies/POL-SUP-003 Supplier Policy v2.3.pdf"
      ],
      "detail": "POL-SUP-003 Supplier Policy v2.3 (1).pdf is an identical duplicate copy of POL-SUP-003 Supplier Policy v2.3.pdf."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "files": [
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-PUR-72 Ledgerline 7.2 User Manual - Purchasing v7.2.3.pdf",
        "03_ledgerline_manuals/MAN-SCR-72 Screen Reference v7.2.3.pdf"
      ],
      "detail": "MAN-PUR-72 lists Warehouse as an optional field on PUR-PR-01 defaulting to WH-MAN-STR, whereas MAN-SCR-72 lists WHS CD as a mandatory field."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
